[statement]
Reduced from a layered request over Alpine v3.24 (`main` and `community`,
2026-11-08): `lua-feedparser`'s closure from v3.23 installed. The world
is empty and `x`, unrelated, is requested, so every installed package
goes. `lua5.4` is removed first, and the packages it needed through names
they provide at a version last: apk removes `readline` before
`lua5.4-libs` in whichever order the installed database lists them and
`lua5.4` states its dependencies: both wait on `musl`, and go before it
in the order of apk's table of names, where `readline`'s own name comes
first (`installed/the-last-removals-go-in-the-order-of-apk-s-table-of-names`).

